   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## kubakub · clay render -> final\n\nFrom a 3D file to a finished facade picture: **scene render** makes the clay view from the file's camera (the\nprojection view) and the ID passes; **regions from id renders** turns them into regions with tags from the 3D\n(front, recess, underside, floors, sections); the **plan** gives each a prompt; **Klein** paints the clay region by\nregion (the clay's light and shape stay: `denoise` 0.7-0.85); the **seam pass** heals the borders; **brightness\ncompensation** evens the projector's light.\n\n**You need:** a scene file with a camera (node 1), Blender 4.x, Flux 2 Klein 4B (nodes 10-12).\nCryptomatte from your own renderer works the same: swap node 2 for *kubakub regions from cryptomatte*.\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
